  {
    "index": 16,
    "created_utc": "2026-11-03T17:19:42.408711+00:00",
    "kind": "decision",
    "previous_sha256": "45be5736efdcb1727a96c760b5fa0d5ff4d95acda052d47531f884092d0b4570",
    "author_id": "/root/ia_l02",
    "decision": {
      "reason": "Retain the original positive-support mixture after complete review of all 30 statistics across the three fixed initial seeds. Execution and scheduled calculations succeed. Generated margins and projection patterns are internally coherent, but no empirical target reference or source-population replay is supplied to identify a scientific correction. The persistent low adjusted age projection and stronger tail-sensitive Pearson association are acknowledged model properties, not dismissed as sampling noise or presented as target validation. Optional trials4301/4302 are skipped because further target-only draws would not resolve transport uncertainty.",
      "kind": "retain",
      "addressed_findings": [
        "Bound actual trial4201 and complete initial delivery feedback in the new final candidate checks artifacts; retained prior frozen candidates unchanged.",
        "Reviewed all 27 marginal/joint diagnostics and E1/E2/E3 in each successful n=3000 run, including all quantiles, positivity and duplicate flags.",
        "Distinguished across-seed variation from the persistent model age projection (E3 0.002986-0.004487) and Pearson/Spearman separation (0.7629-0.7851 versus 0.4781-0.5184).",
        "Kept source projections, rank/arithmetic correlations, individual dispersions and survey SEs distinct. Restored Jansen/Pani age context remains visible without installing a target coefficient.",
        "No scientific generator, model parameter or evidence change; no local row simulation, new retrieval, seed selection or p-value tuning."
      ],
      "remaining_limitations": [
        "Target complete-case age/sex/BMI/glycemia margins and joint law have not been empirically validated; no target reference was supplied.",
        "High-glycemia mixture prevalence, residual dependence, component tails, nonlinear risk and sex/age/BMI gradients remain explicit assumptions; high component is not clinical diabetes.",
        "The low model age projection and stronger arithmetic glucose-HbA1c association may be transport misspecification; supplied evidence cannot adjudicate them.",
        "Source population selection, disease exclusions, weighting, assays, serum/plasma handling and calendar time differ; source replay is not computable.",
        "Three conditional generated draws do not measure source, structural or transport uncertainty; causal, clinical, medication, pregnancy and longitudinal uses remain unassessed."
      ]
    },
    "based_on_feedback_sha256": "7ac76bfb5d522c5b4402f2cdba545e16437eaf92872159507ad112f11c9a29bf"
  },
